From b6d34f64b3049ce8ec0969fe5635d905ca457e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:29:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Odyssey HUD move / resize + full-screen UI (0113 v5)

The compass has no pane of its own: the only pane at x>=900 in log-20/21
is PicStrap (340x720), the right strip that holds the compass, the life
ring and the guide text, so the compass (element 0) is locked by the
name PicStrap and moves the whole strip. All four PicIcon entries in
the logs are accounted for (menu, two moons, life), and the compass is
most likely not a Pane at all (the game reads the camera heading and
draws it directly), so there is nothing else to lock. The log position
is the pane's global matrix, so a Life cluster at (9,40) is NOT a child
of a PicStrap at (1194,0) - dragging the strip leaves the life ring in
place, and life keeps its own element (1). Two PicStrap instances exist
(1194,0) and (780,0); each takes its own pair of slots (idx, idx+4),
so neither drifts.

A moved container must carry its children: a static parent passes the
unchanged flag (w22=0) down, so its children never recompute from the
moved parent. The stub now marks a moved pane's descendants dirty
(bit 4, depth 3, 64 visits) whenever it writes a new matrix, so the
parent's own Calculate carries the children along. The pane itself is
never marked (its own matrix is written directly).
